'" Kalman filter demo `kalman_demo.cpp`
@startuml kalman_demo
title Kalman demo: predict -> update cycle
actor Agent as Main
participant "Example (kalman_demo)" as Example
participant "microla::KalmanFilter" as KF
participant "Sensor" as Sensor
participant "Actuator" as Actuator

Main -> Example: run()
loop each timestep
  Example -> Sensor: read measurement z
  Example -> KF: predict(control)
  KF -> KF: propagate covariance
  Example -> KF: update(z)
  KF -> Example: state estimate x
  Example -> Actuator: apply control from x
end
Example -> Main: final state / log

note right
  Shows typical discrete-time Kalman filter loop
  Use `microla::KalmanFilter` APIs: predict(), update(), state()
end note
@enduml
